- SpType (spectral type): The luminosity class in spectral type (e.g., III, II, Ib) directly indicates giant or supergiant status; V indicates dwarf (main sequence).
- Amag (absolute magnitude): Giants have lower absolute magnitude (brighter intrinsically) than dwarfs of the same spectral type; large Amag (fainter) suggests dwarf, smaller Amag (brighter) suggests giant.

